WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.300
How soap works, your oils, and handling caustic soda safely.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:08.720
This is the video for Module 1 of Soap Making for Small Business.

3
00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:15.880
Every true soap is made from two things. Fats or oils, and a strong alkali called lye.

4
00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:23.340
For bar soap, the lye is sodium hydroxide. In our markets it is sold as caustic soda.

5
00:00:24.590 --> 00:00:31.840
For soft and liquid soap, the lye is potassium hydroxide, often called caustic potash or K O H.

6
00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.890
When oil and lye meet in water, they react. This is called saponification.

7
00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:46.720
Oil and lye become soap and glycerin, a natural moisturiser. Measured correctly, no lye is left in the bar.

8
00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:53.770
With melt-and-pour, you melt a ready soap base. You never touch lye, but the base is costly.

9
00:00:55.020 --> 00:01:04.810
Cold process needs care and about 4 to 6 weeks of curing, but gives the lowest cost per bar and full control. Most small soap businesses choose it.

10
00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:13.950
Palm oil gives a hard, long-lasting bar with creamy lather. It can be 25% to 50% of your recipe.

11
00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:24.820
Palm kernel oil, P K O, adds hardness, strong cleaning and big bubbles. Keep it at 15% to 30%, because too much can be drying.

12
00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:31.020
Shea butter adds a creamy, conditioning feel, at 5% to 15%.

13
00:01:32.270 --> 00:01:37.840
Castor oil boosts the lather, at 3% to 8%. Too much makes soap sticky.

14
00:01:38.190 --> 00:01:42.500
Buy oils that smell fresh. Old oil causes orange spots later.

15
00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:48.660
For example, Bisi in Ibadan plans a test batch of 800 g of oils.

16
00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:55.260
Palm oil is 50%. 800 times 0.50 is 400 g.

17
00:01:56.510 --> 00:02:00.670
Palm kernel oil is 30%. That is 240 g.

18
00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.780
Shea butter is 15%. That is 120 g.

19
00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:17.000
Castor oil is 5%. That is 40 g. Check it: 400 plus 240 plus 120 plus 40 makes 800 g.

20
00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:25.500
Weigh every oil, never use cups. Lye is calculated from the oils, never guessed. You will do that in Module 2.

21
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:33.700
Caustic soda burns skin and can blind you. It does not always sting at once, so treat it like boiling oil.

22
00:02:34.050 --> 00:02:41.030
Halima in Kaduna wants a safe soap corner. She picks a table by the back door, so she can mix lye outside.

23
00:02:42.280 --> 00:02:54.550
She buys sealed goggles for about 2,500 naira, nitrile gloves for about 3,500, and a digital scale for about 6,000. These prices are approximate.

24
00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:58.340
That is about 12,000 naira in total.

25
00:02:58.690 --> 00:03:07.990
She labels a stainless pot and a P P 5 jug soap only. Never aluminium, because lye attacks it. And no one cooks while lye is out.

26
00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:18.260
Step one. Goggles, gloves over the wrists, long sleeves and closed shoes. Children and pets out. Work outdoors or by an open window.

27
00:03:19.510 --> 00:03:25.190
Step two. Weigh cold water, distilled or boiled and cooled, into a heat-safe container.

28
00:03:26.440 --> 00:03:30.490
Step three. Weigh the caustic soda into a separate, dry container.

29
00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:37.930
Step four. In a ventilated spot, slowly pour the caustic soda into the water, stirring gently.

30
00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:45.340
Remember this rule. Never pour water onto caustic soda. It can boil up and splash violently.

31
00:03:46.590 --> 00:03:55.700
Step five. Step back. The solution heats fast and can pass 80 degrees Celsius. Label it, and let it cool where no one can knock it over.

32
00:03:56.950 --> 00:04:07.110
If lye touches your skin, remove the clothing and rinse with cool running water for at least 15 minutes. Do not use vinegar. Water is the correct first treatment.

33
00:04:08.360 --> 00:04:16.870
If it gets in the eyes, rinse with clean running water for at least 15 minutes, holding the eyelids open, and go to a hospital straight away.

34
00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:24.030
If it is swallowed, rinse the mouth, do not make the person vomit, and get medical help immediately.

35
00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:27.980
Keep a bottle of clean water on your table every time you work.

36
00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:41.290
To remember. Weigh, never guess. Cold process needs curing time. Local oils make a good base. Caustic soda goes into water. And store it sealed, labelled, never in a drink bottle.

37
00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:52.370
Now it is your turn. Map five soaps in your market, design your own four-oil recipe, and build a safety station with a first aid card on the wall.

38
00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.660
Continue with the lessons below.
